+### 4.3 list_conversations
+
+- A `list_conversations` request accepts an optional integer `limit` from 1 to 200 and an optional `before` cursor carrying a parseable ISO `updatedAt` and a `sessionId`; malformed fields are rejected and extra fields are ignored ([validated by: validates the list frame and its composite cursor independently of configuration](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L36)).
+- With history enabled, the server answers only when asked with one `conversation_list` containing the authenticated connection user's own metadata, newest first, with ISO timestamps and no conversation content; it forwards the requested page to the store and never takes the user id from the frame ([validated by: answers only the authenticated user with wire summaries and passes the requested page to the store](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L62)).
+- With history disabled, the server answers the request with an `UNSUPPORTED` error instead of a list ([validated by: refuses a list when history is disabled](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L77)).
+- A store unable to list yields `UNSUPPORTED`, while other store failures yield a sanitized `SERVER_ERROR` ([validated by: reports unavailable and failing stores without presenting an empty history](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L81)).
+
 ## 5. Server-to-Client Messages
 
 ### 5.1 connected
diff --git a/src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts b/src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts
